EXPERIMENT 55 – TESTING DYNAMICALLY LOADED WEB ELEMENTS USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to test dynamically loaded web elements using explicit waits.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Open the dynamic loading page.
3. Click the Start button.
4. Create a WebDriverWait of 10 seconds.
5. Wait until the element with ID finish becomes visible using ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated().
6. Read the text and verify that it is Hello World!.
7. Close the browser.
CODE
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.ExpectedConditions;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.WebDriverWait;
import java.time.Duration;

public class Exercise55 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            driver.get(
                "https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dynamic_loading/2");

            driver.findElement(
                By.cssSelector("#start button")).click();

            WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(
                driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));

            WebElement finish = wait.until(
                ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(
                    By.id("finish")));

            System.out.println(
                "Dynamic text : " + finish.getText());

            System.out.println("Verification : "
                + (finish.getText().equals("Hello World!")
                ? "PASS" : "FAIL"));

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- URL: https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dynamic_loading/2
- Button: Start
- Expected text: Hello World!
- Explicit wait: 10 seconds
OUTPUT
Dynamic text : Hello World!
Verification : PASS


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to test dynamically loaded web elements using explicit waits was executed successfully, and the output was verified.
